==Battleground==
*3 [[Metal Snache]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.
*5 [[Metal Snache]]s spawn after 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>, delay 3.33~6.67 seconds<sup>100f~200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Mecha-Bun (Enemy)|Mecha-Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**5 [[Super Metal Hippoe]]s spawn, delay 36.67~40 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,200f</sup>.
**3 [[THE METAL SLOTH]]s spawn, delay 46.67~50 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,500f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Metal Doge]]s spawn, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The best way to complete this stage is to use [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Cleanerbot Cat]] to stall the initial Metal Snaches, then stack [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attackers]] such as [[Cyberpunk Cat]], [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Awakened Mina]] and [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Ballet Cat]]. Unless you bring something like [[Balaluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Piccolan Pasalan]] or [[Wrathful Poseidon (Uber Rare Cat)|Poseidon]], start by blocking the snakes further from the base and killing a few with something like [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Waitress Cat]], who should later die as the Snakes advance, allowing you to stall the rest for an extremely long time just with Cleanerbots. If you have any [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] with Long Distance and any ability that [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|targets Metal]] or [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|Floating]] (except [[Curse]]), make sure to stack them as well.

When you are ready to hit the base, remember that if Mecha Bun darts in the range of your line of Cyberpunks, then all of their attacks will happen immediately one after the other, resulting in a lot of downtime on the slow, so use the [[Ototo Corps#Slow Beam|Slow Beam]] to make it so the Cyberpunks reach Mecha Bun one after the other, resulting in well-spaced attacks that may be unavoidable to anyone who tries to dash in. From there, clearing the stage should be easy enough.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Aoshi Shinomori (Uber Rare Cat)|Aoshi Shinomori]]: If you're lucky enough to have him, Aoshi Shinomori can be extremely useful here.  Stacking 2-3 of them alongside [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can easily permafreeze Mecha-Bun, allowing you to chip away at the Metal peons.
*[[Juri (Uber Rare Cat)|Juri]]: Juri doubles as crowd-control and damage for Mecha-Bun. She lacks issues with peons blocking the way and the slow isn't particularly inconvenient if using Cyberpunk.
*[[Vega (Uber Rare Cat)|Vega]]: Vega's build of Long Distance Metal crowd-control and [[Critical Hit|Critical Hits]] lets him snipe THE METAL SLOTH, nuke or kill Super Metal Hippoe and provide great support for the previous and other metals. He can also deal slight chip damage to Mecha-Bun.
*[[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Hayabusa]]: Hayabusa's Long Distance allows him be stacked, and a stack of Hayabusas can easily clear any Metal enemies with their highly damaging Crits, as well as provide extra damage to Mecha-Bun.
*[[Empress Chronos (Uber Rare Cat)|Empress Chronos]]: A stack of Chronoses can help freeze both Mecha-Bun and the Metal enemies.

